{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/112785","id":3012166126,"node_id":"PR_kwDOAO6SJc6zigHu","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/112785","diff_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/112785.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/112785.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/112785","commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/112785/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/112785/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/112785/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/statuses/6e345f80ec834333dad466d576c6c00a92c51cb4","number":112785,"state":"closed","locked":false,"title":"Integrate `clang-tidy` into CI","user":{"login":"Ivorforce","id":2308167,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIzMDgxNjc=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2308167?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce","html_url":"https://github.com/Ivorforce","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"Clang-tidy is the bigger, more powerful sibling of `clang-format`. The main difference is that `clang-format` parses files in isolation, and focuses on linting features, while `clang-tidy` trudges into the first steps of compilation, and can use more advanced information.\r\n\r\nWe already use `clang-format`. This PR introduces `clang-tidy` (in minimal form).\r\n\r\n### Motivation\r\n\r\nI think we want (need!) `clang-tidy` for its many great codebase-quality related features, such as:\r\n- [Remove unused includes](https://clang.llvm.org/extra/clang-tidy/checks/misc/include-cleaner.html)\r\n- Force use of specific features (e.g. `nullptr` over `NULL`).\r\n- Flag bug-prone syntax or implementations\r\n- Enforce certain naming conventions\r\n- ... and many, many more\r\n\r\n### clang-tidy Initial State\r\n\r\nBuilding on Repiteo's [initial implementation](https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/93271), I focused on getting the \"simplest\" version of clang-tidy integrated that I could.\r\n\r\nHowever, I needed to nerf it severely for it to run:\r\n- All features disabled (except header modernization). \r\n    - Notably, it will still flag some important things, such as unused functions or missing includes\r\n- Whitelist directories to run on. Platform-specific directories fail because of missing header files.\r\n- Unknown warning diagnostics ignored (via https://stackoverflow.com/a/47043282/503822)\r\n\r\nWith everything nerfed, and problems fixed, the following command succeeded (after about 15m of runtime):\r\n\r\n```shell\r\npre-commit run --all-files --hook-stage manual clang-tidy\r\n```\r\n\r\nI also removed `cppcoreguidelines-pro-type-member-init` for good, because it just generated false positives (as far as i can judge - it suggested using `Class some_class{}` instead of `Class some_class` for using the default initializer.\r\n\r\n### CI implementation\r\n\r\n`clang-tidy` makes use of `compile_commands.json` to run properly. That means users will have to have it up-to-date for `pre-commit` to run as expected.\r\nThis is probably not acceptable in the standard workflow, so I kept the `clang-tidy` `pre-commit` hook as manual.\r\n\r\nTo integrate it, I add `compiledb=yes` to the build command of Linux builders, and let the fastest linux builder (Minimal) take the burden of running it. It should not make a difference on the actual runtime of CI.\r\n\r\n### Changes made\r\n\r\nAll necessary because of `clang-tidy` failures:\r\n\r\n- `static` free functions changed to `inline`. `static` forces compile units to keep their own version, leading to unnecessary engine bloat (and an \"unused function\" warning)\r\n- Incorrect `#include <type_traits>` changed to `#include <utility>`\r\n- C-header `#include <stdint.h>` changed to C++ header `#include <cstdint>`. In theory, this should reduce the number of ambiguous/error-prone free functions (but in practice, it doesn't make a difference in stdlib implementations)\r\n\r\n","labels":[{"id":73330066,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWw3MzMzMDA2Ng==","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/enhancement","name":"enhancement","description":"","color":"aaccff","default":true,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":279098009,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwyNzkwOTgwMDk=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/topic:buildsystem","name":"topic:buildsystem","description":"","color":"ffee88","default":false,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":2304948121,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwyMzA0OTQ4MTIx","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/topic:codestyle","name":"topic:codestyle","description":"","color":"ffee88","default":false,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null}],"milestone":{"id":14236899,"node_id":"MI_kwDOAO6SJc4A2Tzj","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/milestones/24","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/milestone/24","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/milestones/24/labels","number":24,"state":"closed","title":"4.7","description":"","creator":{"login":"akien-mga","id":4701338,